+							*background-flash*
+	By default Vim does not wait for this response during startup.  If you
+	see a light-background flash in a dark terminal, set 'termbackgroundwait'
+	in your vimrc to wait briefly before the first screen clear.  For
+	example: >
+		set termbackgroundwait=100
+<	This may delay startup by up to 100 ms.  If the response arrives later,
+	the colors are adjusted then, so a flash may still occur.
 
