@@ -9339,6 +9347,25 @@ A jump table for the options with a short description can be found at |Q_op|.
 		:set term=$TERM
 <	See |termcap|.
 
+					*'termbackgroundwait'* *'tbw'*
+'termbackgroundwait' 'tbw' number (default 0)
+			global
+			{only available when compiled with the |+termresponse|
+			feature}
+	Maximum time in milliseconds to wait for the terminal background color
+	response during interactive startup, before the first screen clear.
+	Zero (the default) defers the query until after startup commands and
+	disables waiting.  A positive value sends the query before the first
+	screen clear.  The value must not be negative.  See |background-flash|
+	for an example.
+
+	Vim only waits when 'background' has not been explicitly set, |t_RB| is
+	not empty, and both input and output are terminals.  Waiting ends early
+	when a response, typed input, or an interrupt is received.  Responses
+	arriving after the timeout are still used to adjust 'background', so
+	this option cannot prevent every flash.  It has no effect in the GUI
+	or after startup.
+
